Vendored from Chocolate Doom, https://github.com/chocolate-doom/chocolate-doom,
upstream commit e6f632a4397023b6b17cc312525a16b2aacd64d6 (shallow clone,
2026-10-19), for music: Doom's MUS songs played on an emulated OPL FM chip
with the IWAD's GENMIDI instruments, as DMX played them on an AdLib or a
Sound Blaster.

From src/: i_oplmusic.c (the OPL music module), midifile.c, midifile.h.
From opl/: opl.c, opl.h, opl_internal.h, opl_queue.c, opl_queue.h (the OPL
library), opl3.c, opl3.h, wf_rom.h (Nuked OPL3, with Chocolate Doom's
"Nuked-OPL3-fast" changes).

Licences: Chocolate Doom's code is GPL-2.0-or-later (COPYING.md here).
Nuked OPL3 (opl3.c, opl3.h, wf_rom.h) is LGPL-2.1-or-later
(LICENSE.LGPL-2.1 here, from https://github.com/nukeykt/Nuked-OPL3), which
may be combined with this GPL program.

Not taken: the SDL, Linux/OpenBSD port-I/O and Windows drivers
(opl_sdl.c, opl_linux.c, opl_obsd.c, opl_win32.c, opl_timer.c,
ioperm_sys.c). This port's driver is csrc/music.c, after opl_sdl.c: it
makes samples when the Rust mixer (src/sound.rs) asks for them.
mus2mid.c comes from doomgeneric (see doomgeneric/NOTE).

rs_compat.h is this port's (force-included by build.rs): the few names
Chocolate Doom's headers have and doomgeneric's lack (PACKED_STRUCT,
SDL_SwapBE16/32, I_Realloc, opl_driver_ver_t).

Local changes, each under #ifdef RS_RICH_DOOM unless noted:
- opl.c: no config.h or SDL.h; the only driver is opl_rs_driver; OPL_Delay
  advances the software driver's clock (OPL_RS_Delay) instead of waiting
  on an SDL condition for the audio thread.
- opl_internal.h: declares opl_rs_driver and OPL_RS_Delay instead of the
  SDL driver.
- i_oplmusic.c: songs are converted (mus2mid) and read in memory, without
  a temporary file; a missing or short GENMIDI lump turns music off
  instead of reading past it; a lump can be given directly (tests);
  music_opl_module and its device list are not const (doomgeneric's
  i_sound.h declares them so).
- midifile.c, midifile.h (not under #ifdef): MIDI_LoadFile reads from
  memory (a MEMFILE, doomgeneric's memio.c) instead of a file name.
Everything else is unmodified.
